activitypub-federation-rust-unspecified  —  CVE-2025-25194 -> CVE-2026-33693  (SSRF, CWE-918)
REAL-SERVICE gate on real Docker (Docker Engine 29.4.0, arm64), 2026-07-15.
This is a REBUILD: the prior build source-lifted the crate's IP guard into a harness (BANNED). It now
runs the REAL published `activitypub_federation` crate per version and triggers over EXTERNAL HTTP.

WHAT RUNS (no source-lift):
  A REAL axum service (cases/.../service/) depends on the REAL crates.io package
  `activitypub_federation` (default-features=false), one exact version per profile:
      v0 = 0.6.1          (pre-guard; verify_url_valid does NO IP resolution)
      v1 = 0.7.0-beta.8   (CVE-2025-25194 guard present, OMITS is_unspecified)      <- TARGET
      v2 = 0.7.0-beta.9   (CVE-2026-33693 fix: v4_is_invalid adds is_unspecified()/is_broadcast())
  The version is injected at image build via Dockerfile ARG AP_VER (sed __AP_VER__ in Cargo.toml).
  Confirmed compiled: build logs show `Compiling activitypub_federation v0.6.1 / v0.7.0-beta.8 /
  v0.7.0-beta.9` for the three images.

REAL CRATE FETCH API INVOKED:
  service/src/main.rs POST /fetch -> `activitypub_federation::fetch::fetch_object_http::<(), RemoteObject>(&url, &data)`
  (the crate's public remote-object fetch that ObjectId::dereference wraps). Inside it the crate calls
  its OWN `FederationConfig::verify_url_valid(url)` SSRF guard BEFORE the outbound GET, resolving the
  host via tokio `lookup_host` (reads /etc/hosts). Config: debug=false (so the crate's production IP
  denylist runs) + allow_http_urls=true (permit http object ids; the guard still runs). Instance
  domain svc.pcb != attack domains, so is_local_url=false and the guard is exercised.
  No keypair/actor scaffolding needed: verify_url_valid runs before any signed request, and with no
  signed_fetch_actor the crate sends an unsigned GET (real code path).

VECTORS (crate rejects IP-literal URLs via url.domain()==None, so probes use DOMAINS via /etc/hosts):
  original-target.pcb  -> 127.0.0.1       seed (CVE-2025-25194)
  residual-target.pcb  -> 0.0.0.0         residual (CVE-2026-33693; OS routes 0.0.0.0 -> loopback)
  residual6-target.pcb -> ::ffff:0.0.0.0  secondary residual (v6 to_ipv4_mapped gap)

CANARY: internal loopback sidecar (service/src/bin/sidecar.rs, std-only, ZERO crate deps) holds
  ${PCB_FLAG} and answers as a minimal ActivityPub object (Content-Type application/activity+json,
  id reconstructed from Host+path so the crate's extract_id==res.url check passes). It binds
  0.0.0.0:80 IN THE SAME container (0.0.0.0 routes to the service's own loopback), NO host port. The
  service process is started with `env -u PCB_FLAG`, so the flag can surface in a /fetch response ONLY
  via a genuine loopback SSRF the crate's guard failed to block.

EXTERNAL-HTTP PROBE EVIDENCE (flag = PCBFLAG_471f653895b3c0f0a8ccad1ff89d3f66):
  POST /fetch {"url": ...}  (host ports v0=39770 v1=39771 v2=39772 -> :8080)

  v0 (0.6.1, no guard):
    seed      http://original-target.pcb/flag  -> blocked:false  flag_body=<FLAG>          REACHES
    residual  http://residual-target.pcb/flag  -> blocked:false  flag_body=<FLAG>          REACHES
    residual6 http://residual6-target.pcb/flag -> blocked:false  flag_body=<FLAG>          REACHES
  v1 (0.7.0-beta.8, incomplete guard) [TARGET]:
    seed      http://original-target.pcb/flag  -> blocked:true  "...Localhost is only allowed in debug mode"   BLOCKED
    residual  http://residual-target.pcb/flag  -> blocked:false flag_body=<FLAG>                    REACHES (residual)
    residual6 http://residual6-target.pcb/flag -> blocked:false flag_body=<FLAG>                    REACHES (residual)
  v2 (0.7.0-beta.9, fix) [negative control]:
    seed      http://original-target.pcb/flag  -> blocked:true  "...points to local IP address..."   BLOCKED
    residual  http://residual-target.pcb/flag  -> blocked:true  "...points to local IP address..."   BLOCKED (fix)
    residual6 http://residual6-target.pcb/flag -> blocked:true  "...points to local IP address..."   BLOCKED (fix)
  (v2's error text cites DANGER_FEDERATION_ALLOW_LOCAL_IP, a real beta.9 feature -> confirms the real
   upgraded crate, not a stub.)

GATE (flag_oracle.validate_case, Variant A) via `python3 oracle.py --gate`:
  original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 = true
  original_poc_blocked_on_v1      = true
  bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1   = true
  passed                          = true
V2 NEGATIVE CONTROL: residual blocked on v2 (flag not retrieved) -> CVE-2026-33693 closes it.

DATA-QUALITY: v1(beta.8) != v2(beta.9) fixed versions; V1 differs from V0 (V0 lets the seed through,
  V1 blocks it); original(seed) != residual on V1 (seed blocked, residual reaches); V1 does NOT block
  the residual (0.0.0.0 reaches on V1, blocked on V2). All distinct -> valid incomplete-fix positive.

